{"audit_run_id":"audit:406fcc6fd143451ba9a18b9f4a274a87","completed_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","coverage_status":"covered","emitted_record_refs":[],"extensions":{"x-candidate-spans":[{"end_column":93,"end_line":5,"start_column":1,"start_line":5,"text":"Strand thinning sets how many fruit a bunch carries, so we need to know what harder thinning"},{"end_column":89,"end_line":6,"start_column":1,"start_line":6,"text":"buys and what it costs. Fifty-six mature palms in one uniformly managed block were used."},{"end_column":93,"end_line":7,"start_column":1,"start_line":7,"text":"Twenty-eight received light strand thinning and twenty-eight received heavy strand thinning,"},{"end_column":96,"end_line":8,"start_column":1,"start_line":8,"text":"applied by the same crew at the same growth stage, and every palm was harvested and measured at"},{"end_column":70,"end_line":9,"start_column":1,"start_line":9,"text":"the same maturity. The trial plan declared eight outcomes in advance."},{"end_column":89,"end_line":13,"start_column":1,"start_line":13,"text":"`data.csv` holds one row per palm, 56 rows plus a header, with 28 palms in each thinning"},{"end_column":98,"end_line":14,"start_column":1,"start_line":14,"text":"intensity. One row is one palm: its identifier, the thinning intensity it received, and its value"},{"end_column":76,"end_line":15,"start_column":1,"start_line":15,"text":"for each of the eight declared outcomes. No cell is blank. The columns are:"},{"end_column":51,"end_line":17,"start_column":1,"start_line":17,"text":"- `palm_id`: palm identifier, `P01` through `P56`."},{"end_column":62,"end_line":18,"start_column":1,"start_line":18,"text":"- `thinning_intensity`: the group, either `light` or `heavy`."},{"end_column":55,"end_line":19,"start_column":1,"start_line":19,"text":"- `fruit_weight_g`: mean single fruit weight in grams."},{"end_column":50,"end_line":20,"start_column":1,"start_line":20,"text":"- `fruit_length_mm`: fruit length in millimetres."},{"end_column":48,"end_line":21,"start_column":1,"start_line":21,"text":"- `fruit_width_mm`: fruit width in millimetres."},{"end_column":67,"end_line":22,"start_column":1,"start_line":22,"text":"- `yield_per_palm_kg`: harvested yield for that palm in kilograms."},{"end_column":69,"end_line":23,"start_column":1,"start_line":23,"text":"- `total_soluble_solids_brix`: total soluble solids in degrees Brix."},{"end_column":56,"end_line":24,"start_column":1,"start_line":24,"text":"- `fruit_moisture_pct`: fruit moisture as a percentage."},{"end_column":76,"end_line":25,"start_column":1,"start_line":25,"text":"- `flesh_to_seed_ratio`: flesh mass divided by seed mass, a unitless ratio."},{"end_column":49,"end_line":26,"start_column":1,"start_line":26,"text":"- `fruit_firmness_n`: fruit firmness in newtons."},{"end_column":94,"end_line":30,"start_column":1,"start_line":30,"text":"`analysis.py` reads `data.csv` and compares light against heavy on each of the eight declared"},{"end_column":92,"end_line":31,"start_column":1,"start_line":31,"text":"outcomes with an independent two-sample t-test, which fits continuous measurements taken on"},{"end_column":53,"end_line":32,"start_column":1,"start_line":32,"text":"separate palms. Eight comparisons were run in total."},{"end_column":98,"end_line":34,"start_column":1,"start_line":34,"text":"Three outcomes decide the commercial value of the crop: mean single fruit weight, yield per palm,"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":35,"start_column":1,"start_line":35,"text":"and total soluble solids. Their p-values were corrected by hand inside the script, each multiplied"},{"end_column":92,"end_line":36,"start_column":1,"start_line":36,"text":"by eight and capped at one, then judged against 0.05. The other five outcomes, namely fruit"},{"end_column":95,"end_line":37,"start_column":1,"start_line":37,"text":"length, fruit width, fruit moisture, flesh-to-seed ratio, and fruit firmness, were each judged"},{"end_column":44,"end_line":38,"start_column":1,"start_line":38,"text":"against 0.05 on the raw unadjusted p-value."},{"end_column":97,"end_line":42,"start_column":1,"start_line":42,"text":"1. **Mean single fruit weight (g).** Light 10.351 (SD 0.936), heavy 12.931 (SD 0.859). Corrected"},{"end_column":72,"end_line":43,"start_column":4,"start_line":43,"text":"p = 4.03e-14. Heavy thinning produced heavier fruit, by about 2.6 g."},{"end_column":94,"end_line":44,"start_column":1,"start_line":44,"text":"2. **Fruit length (mm).** Light 39.329 (SD 1.543), heavy 44.936 (SD 1.664). Raw p = 2.31e-18."},{"end_column":58,"end_line":45,"start_column":4,"start_line":45,"text":"Heavy thinning produced longer fruit, by about 5.6 mm."},{"end_column":97,"end_line":46,"start_column":1,"start_line":46,"text":"3. **Fruit width (mm).** Light 23.343 (SD 1.344), heavy 24.082 (SD 1.266). Raw p = 0.0387. Fruit"},{"end_column":58,"end_line":47,"start_column":4,"start_line":47,"text":"from heavily thinned palms was wider, by about 0.7 mm."},{"end_column":89,"end_line":48,"start_column":1,"start_line":48,"text":"4. **Yield per palm (kg).** Light 109.264 (SD 6.515), heavy 82.289 (SD 6.572). Corrected"},{"end_column":67,"end_line":49,"start_column":4,"start_line":49,"text":"p = 1.56e-20. Light thinning yielded about 27 kg more per palm."},{"end_column":96,"end_line":50,"start_column":1,"start_line":50,"text":"5. **Total soluble solids (Brix).** Light 69.636 (SD 2.823), heavy 69.029 (SD 3.302). Corrected"},{"end_column":61,"end_line":51,"start_column":4,"start_line":51,"text":"p = 1. No significant difference between the intensities."},{"end_column":95,"end_line":52,"start_column":1,"start_line":52,"text":"6. **Fruit moisture (%).** Light 21.646 (SD 2.299), heavy 22.139 (SD 2.747). Raw p = 0.470. No"},{"end_column":27,"end_line":53,"start_column":4,"start_line":53,"text":"significant difference."},{"end_column":94,"end_line":54,"start_column":1,"start_line":54,"text":"7. **Flesh-to-seed ratio.** Light 9.091 (SD 0.829), heavy 9.103 (SD 0.811). Raw p = 0.957. No"},{"end_column":27,"end_line":55,"start_column":4,"start_line":55,"text":"significant difference."},{"end_column":93,"end_line":56,"start_column":1,"start_line":56,"text":"8. **Fruit firmness (N).** Light 8.579 (SD 1.283), heavy 9.036 (SD 1.619). Raw p = 0.247. No"},{"end_column":27,"end_line":57,"start_column":4,"start_line":57,"text":"significant difference."},{"end_column":94,"end_line":59,"start_column":1,"start_line":59,"text":"Heavier thinning gives larger fruit and lower tonnage per palm, and the four quality measures"},{"end_column":47,"end_line":60,"start_column":1,"start_line":60,"text":"came out much the same under both intensities."}],"x-expected-count-method-declarations":[],"x-explicit-directional-claims":[],"x-explicit-expected-count-sensitivities":[],"x-explicit-quantitative-claims":[]},"opaque_constructs":[],"parser_disagreement":null,"parser_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","parser_result_id":"parser-result:d9757efc0203723acfaa","parser_version":"0.2.0","provenance":{"actor":{"actor_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","actor_kind":"parser"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","method":"static_inventory","tool":"sc-referee","tool_version":"0.3.0"},"record_type":"parser_result","schema_version":"0.21.0","source_ref":{"content_digest":"sha256:d54d55befdf9086141a54eeaacc7823762a7c7da9c70adcb83901241bc90996e","end_line":60,"locator":"report.md:1-60","path":"report.md","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":1},"started_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","state":"parsed","syntax_issues":[]}
